122567	122686	122397	122397	he	2415	“ Will you repeat to your sister when she is recovered , what I have been telling you?—Let me be a little lightened too in her opinion as well as in yours . You tell me that she has forgiven me already . Let me be able to fancy that a better knowledge of my heart , and of my present feelings , will draw from her a more spontaneous , more natural , more gentle , less dignified , forgiveness . Tell her of my misery and my penitence — tell her that my heart was never inconstant to her , and if you will , that at this moment she is dearer to me than ever . ”
